# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository, and check it out as LF on every
# platform, matching the sibling projects. Without this, line endings fall back to each
# developer's `core.autocrlf`: a Windows checkout gets a CRLF worktree while rustfmt
# writes LF, so `cargo fmt --check` rewrites whole files and the gates in
# .githooks/pre-commit can never pass there. The hooks themselves are shell scripts, and
# a CRLF one fails to run at all under Git Bash. `eol=lf` is the operative part —
# `text=auto` alone still yields CRLF worktrees on Windows. Binary files stay untouched,
# since Git still auto-detects them.
* text=auto eol=lf
